-- ============================================================================
-- Migration 69 DOWN: no-op.
--
-- Migration 69 defines the `source_verdict` edge table as
-- ``TYPE RELATION FROM source TO source`` (the shape Track Z's contradiction
-- judge needs) and adds its fields (`verdict`, `confidence`, `reasoning`,
-- `judge_model`, `created_at`). It is a forward-only schema definition with no
-- faithful inverse (mirrors migrations 66/67/68's down):
--   * reverting `source_verdict` to TYPE ANY would re-break
--     ``RELATE source -> source_verdict -> source`` — exactly the correctness 69
--     establishes; and
--   * `source_verdict` is a DERIVED, regenerated projection (the judge clears and
--     re-relates a pair's verdict) — the edge table holds no canonical state
--     worth a destructive rollback, and on this corpus it is empty until the
--     judge runs.
-- 69 deliberately does NOT touch the app-side `claim`/`contradicts` tables, so
-- there is nothing of theirs to restore here either.
-- Down intentionally does nothing; mirrors migrations 66/67/68's down convention.
-- ============================================================================
